1
00:00:00,395 --> 00:00:02,895
(Sheldon:)...I would request
that you that add this.

2
00:00:03,064 --> 00:00:04,064
(Penny:)What is it?

3
00:00:05,024 --> 00:00:09,694
(Sheldon:)You're kidding, right?
It's a bust of Sir Isaac Newton.

4
00:00:10,905 --> 00:00:13,245
(Penny:)Oh, sure, sure.
Yeah, very Christmassy.

5
00:00:13,408 --> 00:00:17,748
Excuse me, it's much more Christmassy
than anything you've put on the tree.

6
00:00:17,912 --> 00:00:19,832
LEONARD:
Here we go.

7
00:00:20,039 --> 00:00:24,839
December 25th, 1642, Julian calendar,
Sir Isaac Newton is born.

8
00:00:25,003 --> 00:00:27,753
(Sheldon:)Jesus, on the other hand,
was actually born in the summer.

9
00:00:27,922 --> 00:00:31,422
(Sheldon:)His birthday was moved to coincide
with the traditional pagan holiday...

10
00:00:31,593 --> 00:00:35,343
(Sheldon:)...that celebrated the winter solstice
with lit fires and slaughtered goats.

11
00:00:35,513 --> 00:00:37,393
(Sheldon:)Which, frankly, sounds like more fun...

12
00:00:37,557 --> 00:00:40,807
(Sheldon:)...than 12 hours of church
with my mother followed by a fruitcake.

13
00:00:41,102 --> 00:00:43,692
(Leonard:)Merry Newtonmas, everyone.

14
00:00:43,855 --> 00:00:47,775
(Sheldon:)I sense that's not sincere,
although I have no idea why.

15
00:00:47,942 --> 00:00:50,942
No, it's fine. Sir Isaac can go
next to this candy cane.

16
00:00:51,112 --> 00:00:53,782
(Sheldon:)No, Isaac goes at the top of the tree.

17
00:00:53,948 --> 00:00:56,578
(Leonard:)-No, he doesn't.
-I understand.

18
00:00:56,743 --> 00:00:59,533
(Sheldon:)You dispute Newton's claim
that he invented calculus...

